body='''# Independent custom vector revision 1 source review

Recommendation: suitable for finite original-source integration with 37 exact scalar conformance families and 296 port instances deferred. No structural blocker was found for this receipt. Root must provide its own substantive review, literal pins and repository integration gates. This peer review makes no acceptance increment.

Producer receipt: `261d2be00ae6152fbbad9fc6c540ae96d0ff653198e9ae3ea7533878be7de8e1`.
Public statement: `VeriTile.Bench.TritonBenchG.VectorAdditionCustom.Native.vector_addition_custom_native_source_outcomes`.
Statement SHA: `cf664860c1a6ec09372f7f7a4624dc93c1acac42875db6170666b825e7d07a84`.

## Original host and complete integer domain

I read the original Python, all seven proposed modules, frozen dtype/ABI/source evidence, exact scope/numerical proposal and adapter. The wrapper retains empty_like(a), c.size(0), BLOCK16, ceil-div of the original first dimension, launch and the identical allocated return. It adds no source CUDA guard, same-device guard, y-shape/extent check or contiguity requirement. Rank zero fails after allocation. Output shape, dtype, device, offsets, actual preserve-format strides and initial exterior frame are retained unconditionally under the ordinary allocation contract.

The source length is the first output shape dimension, independent of numel. Actual CPU metadata `(2^31,0)` has zero storage/null data_ptr but a first dimension 2^31 and host grid 2^27. The formal theorem constructs return of the same output and unchanged allocated memory for this dimension under ordinary successful setup, with no access, scalar, CUDA, numel-equality or no-wrap premise. This path was independently instantiated in Lean with shape `[2^31,0]`.

Every nonnegative signed64 dimension remains represented. The annotated size ABI is i32 regardless of the host integer: installed PyLong_AsLong succeeds on the declared domain and int32 assignment narrows modulo 2^32. Grid calculation uses the unnarrowed dimension; offset multiplication/addition wrap at i32; the mask compares signed32; pointers sign-extend offsets before width scaling and u64 wrap. At exactly 2^31 every mask is false. Above it, negative addresses and repeated requests remain explicit. The independent symbolic grid regression proves gridSupported n iff n<=(2^31-1)*16, and the installed signed-int tuple parser rejects larger grids before pointer extraction. There is no silently imposed n<2^31 domain.

## Typed kernel, actual memory and outcomes

Every program executes all active x loads, then all active y loads, then scalar arithmetic and output stores. Source statements, raw TTIR, LLVM/PTX arithmetic and a compiled-C/reference audit agree on the finite requests. Fresh output separates stores from both inputs; x/y overlap is unrestricted. Loaded words are sampled from the initial allocated snapshot in an independent plan, and the correspondence proof carries preservation of those inputs through execution. Repeated overlapping output requests produce a mathematical ownership observation rather than a fabricated native race result. Independent Lean regressions check repeated addresses at pid2^28, their active masks, and their conflict with an already owned span.

The scalar implementation reuses installed shared-vector finite proofs. The 1024 field in the one-cell scalar parameters is not used in scalar computation; actual custom indexing is16. Independent backward fingerprints of all189 original custom frontend stored-value graphs match the frozen shared-vector graphs, retaining exact typed load leaves, constants, opcodes, conversions and destination type. Only SSA names, source locations and16/1024 tensor length are normalized. Six of those typed routes fail the pinned backend and are retained as setup outcomes;183 backend routes are admitted. Partial float-to-integer conversions are observed before a value can be stored. The fallback policies in inherited functions cannot become arbitrary stored values. Integer-only arithmetic, raw bool packing and ordinary byte encoding remain concrete/trusted scalar storage boundaries, not numerical waivers.

Metadata separates Torch raw data/storage pointers from actual successful extracted kernel pointers. TensorBinding.extractedPointer binds Buffer.data to the actual mapped launch pointer on successful setup; mappedData connects it to the mapped allocation and tensor element offset. Buffer permissions are indexed by current launch device rather than allocation owner. An independent regression confirms owner device0 with denied permissions does not authorize a read. Native-address memory is the declared ordinary typed-memory primitive boundary: coherent initial typed loads, pure local packing/stores and local frame laws, without an arbitrary tagged-carrier roundtrip axiom. No canonical-coordinate representation is mandated by this review, and no compiler/MMU correctness is inferred.

Unconditional metadata fields do not assert an extraction Result.ok or any successful native operation. On a branch where pointer extraction is not entered or fails, those unused total fields may be completed arbitrarily subject to ordinary metadata equations. In particular, raw data_ptr/storageBase completion with permissions false does not add a CUDA/source guard. Actual successful extraction must use the actual mapped pointer. The parent and the focused pointer reviewer independently examined this interpretation; no actual-data counterexample was identified. This report does not count their witness executions as my own validation.

Returned bytes are described by an independent reverse last-store formula and pure width-specific packing; all other bytes retain the allocated snapshot. Returned metadata names the same allocator result. Missing bytes, inaccessible spans, invalid input encodings, undefined conversions and conflicting stores are mathematical observations only. They assert no native trap, rollback, postfailure memory, race winner or universal launch reachability. The source/metadata/typed-memory primitive boundary is explicit and contains no final-value or launch-success oracle.

## Exact admission, authority and preserved history

The original22x22 dtype matrix is retained:195 binder failures,64 target-signature failures,36 addition failures,6 backend failures and183 backend compilations. Binder argument precedence, including unsupported fnuz x with an unmapped y dtype, matches the actual binder. Native context/setup is independently fallible. Compilation, signed grid parsing, pointer packing and enqueue are modeled in their source-grounded order, with diagnostic wording outside the claim.

All4,498 schema2 cases were checked against the native route records. The183 exact2^31 return cases require zero numerical ports. The returned/undefined-conversion partitions bind all and only the source profile operations:296 instances across37 families, on actual active source words and exact operand/result/configuration paths. Every required-port omission was independently rejected. Undefined conversion is never waived as numerical uncertainty. Stage, dtype and branch inventory links, public statement SHA and unchanged validators pass.

The old bounded custom five-module/616-port package is historical only. None of its modules occurs in the current seven-module source map, current catalog source hashes, dependency closure or active declaration/authority. Current scalar dependencies are installed shared-vector sources. Historical receipt/source evidence remains frozen and preserved; it does not confer current acceptance.

## Independent validation

- Independently rebuilt seven exact modules using a fresh /tmp overlay. All seven object hashes exactly match the frozen producer outputs.44 clean-axiom and six noncircular checks passed. All seven producer source/attempt/log/object sets and all1,778 candidate artifacts remain unchanged.
- Recursively captured200 project source/object pairs and37 direct external objects before building; producer source/object sets and hashes agree. Every dependency stayed unchanged through finalization. No repository or Git edits were made.
- Replayed484 original-AST dtype configurations and14 ABI/backend profiles. Results and991 raw/frontend/backend/executable-PTX artifacts agree after source-path normalization. PTX debug diffs are retained separately after checking no later executable entry/function.189 backward scalar fingerprints independently match shared-vector IR.
- Recompiled and reran22,272 C/reference finite-address checks,15 original-wrapper AST stub traces,6 real small CPU metadata cases, and7 exact installed grid-parser checks with downstream pointer-failure instrumentation. All structured results equal the frozen producer evidence. The zero-numel huge-shape examples allocate no large storage.
- Independently extracted and compiled installed extractI32 source, checked all14 declared extent boundaries, and verified2^63 produces OverflowError outside the declared signed64 dimension domain. The ABI replay itself also retains the frozen inherited extractor hash.
- Compiled a new Lean theorem comparing all484 freshly replayed admission results with NativeAdmission; the complete matrix and clean-axiom check passed.
- Six independent Lean regressions passed: exact grid threshold; signed-minimum discontinuity and negative pointer reentry; repeated native request; output conflict observation; ownership not granting access; zero-numel/huge-first-dimension original host return. The first reviewer attempt had a namespace-qualification error in the final regression and was rejected by the clean-axiom check. Its source/log/record remain preserved; the corrected second attempt passed.
- Twenty adapter/queue mutations were rejected, using all1,778 actual frozen artifact entries and an explicitly synthetic review fixture: altered sources/helpers/dependencies/runtime/IR/scope, bad pins, conflicting authority, producer self-review, wrong subject/status, path escape, omitted/changed numerical bindings. Whole-queue equality passed on the isolated additive fixture and prior authority was unchanged. This does not replace root integration gates.
- The first IR comparison attempt normalized each ABI directory but missed that ABI debug locations reference the separate native source-prefix directory. The exact failed script/log/full diff are retained. The second comparison adds only that path normalization and passes; no executable difference was discarded.

No GPU launch, live native pointer permission measurement or native scalar numerical validation occurred. All numerical authority remains explicitly deferred. The pinned environment is CUDA sm90, Torch2.13.0+cu130, Triton3.7.1, debug=false and default source launch settings. All producer and reviewer failures are preserved. Work was confined to the new review directory.
'''
